Jerry,

When printing via TCP/IP, are you using the Telnet Symbiont or the
LPR/LPD Symbiont?  If you are using the LPR/LPD symbion make sure that
the destination print queue on the Jet Direct is "text" (case sensitive)
for plain old text files from SYS$PRINT or "raw" (case sensitive) for
things like PostScript files.

I prefer to use the Telnet Symbiont because it gives you full formatting
control over your print job, just like you get with a direct parallel
port, serial port or LAT print queue.  LPR/LPD, on the other hand, has
some serious problems with job formatting when printing to a Jet
Direct.  The reason for this is that the Jet Direct has no spooling area
to hold the data for the print job.  The control file that tells how to
format the job is sent after the data is sent.  Since the Jet Direct
cannot buffer the whole job to receive and process the control file you
will have jobs coming out that are not properly formatted.

NOTE: Printing via the Telnet Symbiont requires that the destination
port be set to "9100" when printing to a Jet Direct.


As for books on VMS systems admin, well, look at the VMS documentation
set.  There is a two volume set of System Administration commands and
guidelines for systems admin.  I just packed my set away for an
impending move and I cannot get you the exact titles right now.


